[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["override the driver's route judgment" "override the driver's on-road safety judgment" "override driver's on-road safety judgment" "finalize the traffic-navigation decision" "finalize the route decision" "directly control vehicle navigation"], :adr/id 2799009331, :actor/domain :transport/hand-pedal-vehicle-dispatch, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-trip-record :schedule-dispatch-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-maintenance-order], :actor/hard-checks [:no-driver :unverified-permit :op-not-allowlisted :no-actuation :route-navigation-override :unknown-vehicle :vehicle-wrong-driver :invalid-cost], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "9331", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799009331: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 9331 Hand and Pedal Vehicle Drivers dispatch/logistics-scheduling coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the ISCO-08 occupation-classification track (sibling to\nthe `cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 9331\n-- Hand and Pedal Vehicle Drivers** only (rickshaw/pedicab/hand-cart\noperators).\n\nThis was dispatched as one of 8 parallel sibling retry-batch agents;\nthis specific ISCO code was confirmed via a fresh `gh api\nrepos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9331` 404 check to have no\npre-existing repository before any work began (a genuinely fresh\nscaffold, unlike some sibling agents in the same batch that were\nrecovering an already-created empty repo or an abandoned local\nscaffold).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"9331\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"9331\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Hand and Pedal Vehicle Drivers\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`. This ADR and\nits companion registry edit promote the `9331` entry to `:implemented`.\n\n**Pedal/hand-cart-vehicle safety dimension.** Hand and Pedal Vehicle\nDrivers in this domain (rickshaw/pedicab/hand-cart operators) navigate\nroads/streets under their own power -- real physical-safety stakes\n(traffic collision, fatigue). This actor is deliberately scoped to\n**dispatch and logistics scheduling coordination ONLY -- it never\noperates the vehicle, and it never finalizes a route/traffic-navigation\ndecision or overrides a driver's on-road safety judgment**. Those\nactions are a hard, permanent block in the governor, independent of\nconfidence and independent of which op was proposed -- never\nauto-commit-eligible, never merely gated behind human escalation. The\nclosed op allowlist itself never includes any op that directly\nfinalizes a route/traffic-navigation decision or overrides a driver's\non-road safety judgment; on top of that, an independent content-based\nscope-exclusion check on the proposal's free-text fields hard-blocks\nany attempt to smuggle such a decision through an otherwise-allowlisted\nop. This mirrors the same class of guardrail this fleet has already\napplied to other domains with an irreversible physical/safety stake\n(e.g. the sibling ISCO-08 8321 Motorcycle Drivers actor,\n`cloud-itonami-isco-8321`, and its precedent that decisions directly\ntouching a person's on-road safety must always exclude the closed op\nallowlist rather than merely be gated behind a confidence threshold).\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313)\n(Accounting Associate Professionals: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/\n`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set --\nCODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, LICENSE\n(AGPL-3.0-or-later), README.md, SECURITY.md, docs/business-model.md,\ndocs/operator-guide.md), freshly cloned and read in full in this\nsession (`git/deps.edn` coordinates for `io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`\ncopied verbatim, same `:git/sha` pin).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9331` as an OSS\ndispatch/logistics-coordination actor for independent hand/pedal-vehicle\n(rickshaw/pedicab/hand-cart) dispatch practices, following the SAME\ngoverned-actor architecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor\nin this fleet: **Hand/Pedal Vehicle Dispatch Advisor ⊣\nHandPedalDispatchGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with\nan independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger. `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` is deliberately NOT a `deps.edn` dependency of this actor\nrepo -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry depends on\nit.\n\nThis actor is **dispatch/logistics-scheduling coordination ONLY, never\nvehicle-operation authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise,\nsimulate exercising, or propose exercising any decision that directly\nfinalizes a route/traffic-navigation decision or overrides a driver's\non-road safety judgment.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-trip-record` -- trip/fare/incident-report data logging\n- `:schedule-dispatch-operation` -- driver-roster/route-assignment\n  scheduling proposal (an administrative scheduling proposal, never a\n  turn-by-turn route/traffic-navigation decision)\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a vehicle-defect/road-hazard/\n  driver-fatigue concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-maintenance-order` -- vehicle maintenance procurement\n  proposal\n\n`handpedaldispatch.governor/closed-op-allowlist` is a closed four-op\n`#{}` set -- any `:op` outside it is unconditionally rejected as\n`:op-not-allowlisted` (`handpedaldispatch.governor-test/hard-on-op-\nnot-allowlisted`, exercised end-to-end through the actor graph by\n`handpedaldispatch.actor-test/holds-an-out-of-allowlist-op`), and the\nmock advisor (`handpedaldispatch.advisor/mock-advisor`) can only ever\nemit whatever `:op` the request itself carried (its `infer` function\nmerges the request through unchanged, with no path to synthesize a\nforeign op).\n\n### Eight HARD governor checks (`handpedaldispatch.governor/hard-violations`, permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **No driver** -- the driver (`driver-record`) must be independently\n   registered; an unregistered driver is a HARD block (`:no-driver`).\n2. **Unverified permit** -- a registered driver whose\n   `:permit-verified?` is not `true` is a HARD block\n   (`:unverified-permit`) -- this directly implements the task's\n   \"driver/permit record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action\" invariant. Never trusts a driver record's mere\n   presence in the store as sufficient; the permit-verification flag\n   is checked independently.\n3. **Op not allowlisted** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:op-not-allowlisted`).\n4. **No actuation** -- `:effect` must be `:propose`; any other value\n   is a HARD block (`:no-actuation`) -- the governor never dispatches\n   hardware itself and never operates the vehicle.\n5. **Route/traffic-navigation scope exclusion** -- independent of the\n   op-allowlist check, any proposal whose string-valued fields (e.g.\n   `:rationale`) name a route/traffic-navigation finalization action or\n   a driver-safety-judgment override action\n   (`handpedaldispatch.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases`: \"override the\n   driver's route judgment\", \"override the driver's on-road safety\n   judgment\", \"override driver's on-road safety judgment\", \"finalize\n   the traffic-navigation decision\", \"finalize the route decision\",\n   \"directly control vehicle navigation\") is a HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:route-navigation-override`), evaluated unconditionally on content\n   regardless of confidence or op. Full action PHRASES only,\n   deliberately never bare nouns such as \"route\" or \"traffic\" -- see\n   the self-trip guard section below.\n6. **Unknown vehicle** -- a `:coordinate-maintenance-order` proposal\n   must cite a REGISTERED vehicle (`vehicle-record`); a nil lookup is a\n   HARD block (`:unknown-vehicle`).\n7. **Vehicle wrong driver** -- a registered vehicle belonging to a\n   DIFFERENT driver than the requesting driver is a HARD block\n   (`:vehicle-wrong-driver`).\n8. **Invalid cost** -- a `:coordinate-maintenance-order` proposal whose\n   `:estimated-cost` is present but not a number is a HARD block\n   (`:invalid-cost`) -- defensive against a malformed/adversarial\n   proposal bypassing the cost-ceiling escalation check below by\n   supplying a non-numeric cost.\n\n### One always-escalate op, one cost-threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (`handpedaldispatch.governor/always-escalate-ops`).\n  Vehicle-defect / road-hazard / driver-fatigue concerns are never\n  auto-resolved.\n- a `:coordinate-maintenance-order` proposal whose `:estimated-cost`\n  exceeds the registered vehicle's `:maintenance-cost-ceiling` always\n  needs human sign-off, independent of confidence (inclusive boundary\n  verified by `handpedaldispatch.governor-test/ok-at-exact-maintenance-\n  ceiling-boundary` -- exactly-at-ceiling auto-commits, above-ceiling\n  escalates per `handpedaldispatch.governor-test/escalates-maintenance-\n  order-above-cost-ceiling`, exercised end-to-end by\n  `handpedaldispatch.actor-test/interrupts-then-approves-over-ceiling-\n  maintenance-order`). This is deliberately an ESCALATE, not a HARD\n  block -- a cost overrun is a business decision a human can approve,\n  unlike the route/traffic-navigation scope exclusion which is\n  permanently blocked.\n- advisor confidence below `handpedaldispatch.governor/confidence-\n  floor` (0.6) also escalates, for any op\n  (`handpedaldispatch.governor-test/escalates-low-confidence`).\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"route\", \"traffic\") can accidentally match inside the mock advisor's\nown default rationale text for a legitimate proposal, self-blocking the\nactor's own happy path -- exactly the risk this vertical's own\nvocabulary (every dispatch/schedule proposal necessarily mentions a\n`:route-assignment` field and words like \"route\" in ordinary scheduling\ncontext) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`handpedaldispatch.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases` is phrased\nexclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare nouns, and\n`handpedaldispatch.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-\nself-trip` is a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the\nclosed allowlist, driven through the default mock advisor\n(`handpedaldispatch.advisor/mock-advisor`) with realistic field values\nincluding a `:route-assignment \"route-42\"` field on the\n`:schedule-dispatch-operation` request, never trips\n`:route-navigation-override`. Green on this session's test run -- the\nguard was never observed to self-trip during verification.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"9331\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to the\n  real repository (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-\n  isco-9331` / `cloud-itonami-isco-9331`), and `maturity-summary`'s\n  implemented count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the\n  registry via `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before\n  the edit, not assumed, to account for concurrent sibling agents\n  landing changes to the same registry file in this batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`) run against the actual pushed,\n  freshly re-cloned repository: 20 tests, 46 assertions, 0 failures, 0\n  errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/raw-output` and in\n  the task report.\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to this actor's own\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  depends on it.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-route-change` or\n  `:finalize-dispatch-route` that is merely gated behind\n  `always-escalate-ops` rather than structurally excluded: rejected\n  outright per the task's explicit guidance and this fleet's\n  established precedent for irreversible-safety-stake decisions -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a route\n  or traffic-navigation decision exists in the code path and is merely\n  deferred to a human gate. This actor coordinates dispatch/logistics\n  scheduling only; the capability to finalize on-road navigation or\n  override a driver's safety judgment must not exist at all, hence a\n  hard, permanent, content-based block rather than an escalation gate.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"route\" \"traffic\"\n  \"navigation\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above -- this actor's own domain necessarily mentions\n  \"route\" and similar words in ordinary dispatch/schedule rationale\n  text (e.g. a `:route-assignment` field on a scheduling proposal), so\n  a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals. Phrased instead as full finalization/execution action\n  phrases, with a dedicated regression test proving the default\n  advisor's own proposals never self-trip.\n- A numeric confidence-only gate for `:log-trip-record` /\n  `:schedule-dispatch-operation` / `:coordinate-maintenance-order` (no\n  driver-provenance/permit-verification or route/traffic-finalization\n  content checks): rejected as insufficient -- confidence measures the\n  advisor's certainty about the proposal it chose to make, not whether\n  that proposal cites an unverified driver or smuggles a route-\n  finalization decision in its free text, which is exactly why the\n  driver-verification and scope-exclusion checks exist as independent,\n  content-based, permanent HARD blocks regardless of confidence.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-trip-record`** -- trip/fare/incident-report data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered AND permit-verified\n   driver (HARD-blocked otherwise by checks 1/2). Not a route/\n   navigation decision or vehicle-operation action in any respect -- it\n   is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-dispatch-operation`** -- driver-roster/route-assignment\n   *scheduling* proposal (administrative logistics, e.g. \"assign driver\n   to the 08:00-16:00 shift for cart-042\"), never a turn-by-turn route/\n   traffic-navigation decision. Any free text that names a route/\n   traffic-navigation finalization action or a driver-safety-judgment\n   override is independently HARD-blocked by check 5 regardless of\n   what op was used to carry it.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a vehicle-defect/road-hazard/\n   driver-fatigue concern to a human; ALWAYS escalates\n   (`always-escalate-ops`, unconditionally, at every confidence level),\n   NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which\n   the robot may surface a safety observation, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself.\n4. **`:coordinate-maintenance-order`** -- vehicle maintenance\n   procurement proposal. Requires an independently registered vehicle\n   belonging to the requesting driver (HARD-blocked otherwise by checks\n   6/7), and any proposal above the registered\n   `:maintenance-cost-ceiling` always escalates to a human, independent\n   of confidence. Not a vehicle-operation or route-navigation action --\n   it is a purchasing-logistics action.\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, finalizes\na route or traffic-navigation decision, or overrides a driver's on-road\nsafety judgment -- confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist\nitself (`handpedaldispatch.governor/closed-op-allowlist`), (b) the\ncontent-based, phrase-driven scope-exclusion check independent of the\n`:op` field (`handpedaldispatch.governor/scope-violation?`,\n`handpedaldispatch.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases`), tested directly\nagainst `governor/check`\n(`handpedaldispatch.governor-test/hard-on-route-navigation-override-\nattempt`, `handpedaldispatch.governor-test/hard-on-traffic-navigation-\nfinalization-attempt`), and (c) the dedicated self-trip regression\nproving the default mock advisor's own proposals, across all four\nallowlisted ops, never accidentally trip that same block\n(`handpedaldispatch.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-\nself-trip`).\n", :test/raw-output "Running tests in #{\"test\"}\n\nTesting handpedaldispatch.actor-test\n\nTesting handpedaldispatch.governor-test\n\nRan 20 tests containing 46 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n", :adr/date "2026-07-17", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-maintenance-order maintenance-cost-ceiling}", :test/counts "{:total 20, :assertions 46, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Hand and Pedal Vehicle Dispatch Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :driver-permit-verification :vehicle-verification :closed-op-allowlist :maintenance-cost-threshold-escalation :route-traffic-navigation-block], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-9331", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9331", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9331], :test/simulator :handpedaldispatch.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-9331 — Hand and Pedal Vehicle Drivers Dispatch/Logistics-Scheduling Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-9331}]